{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"generated":true}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"EntityCollapse","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"enum","roleHeading":"Enumeration","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are one failure mode; the other is a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"singleton"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — an entity an app holds","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fresh installs, two singletons have "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"different"}]},{"type":"text","text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"([E]) -> [E]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API."}]},{"text":"The determinism requirement","type":"heading","anchor":"The-determinism-requirement","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver must be a pure function of ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"replicated content"}]},{"text":" — never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistentModelID"},{"text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other’s, and after sync "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"both"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" rows are gone."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It must also be idempotent — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(collapse(rows))"},{"type":"text","text":" must keep the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"IDs as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(rows)"},{"type":"text","text":". This is checked with an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assert"},{"type":"text","text":" in debug builds."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows","text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver’s output is read as ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each should contain"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"surviving","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ID are all updated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are lost.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB"},{"type":"text","text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentati